WEBVTT

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.560
I'm still over 50 cards...

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.480
Um, then...

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.740
But this way, the balance...

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.280
Hey, Aichi!

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.360
Owww...

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.610
Yeesh! What are you thinking?!

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.650
What's the idea of kicking me out?!

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.930
If you have to give somebody the 
boot, wouldn't Flogal go before me?!

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.660
What was that?!

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.820
Unlike you, I've got a stand trigger!

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.930
Just because you've got a little more 
power is no reason to be full of yourself!

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.800
W-What'd you say?!

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:52.720
What?!

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.620
H-Hold on!

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.550
Both of you, it's not 
good to fight! Calm down!

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.200
Then what about me?

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.530
That's right!

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:04.170
You don't understand anything!

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.800
I'm the most powerful you've got!

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.990
Don't you know how important 
a critical trigger is?!

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.060
Aichi...

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:16.100
Emi? I'm a little busy right 
now. Talk to me later!

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.640
Aichi!

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.920
Aichi!!

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.230
Aichi!!

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:25.780
Enough! I told you I'll talk to you later!

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.390
Yeesh! You're talking in your sleep!

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:31.960
Emi?

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.560
Oh, for goodness sake!

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.890
You're not at home!

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.750
"Emi!"

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:42.000
"I'm a little busy right now!"

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.670
"Talk to me later!"

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.130
M-Morikawa! Isaki!

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.390
Emi!!

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:53.050
Please forget about that!

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.060
No way!

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.670
Well, just goes to show that 
you can't wake up without me.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.800
I-I'm totally jealous of you, Brother!

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:39.250
Good morning...

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.760
Good morning!

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.820
Huh? You're up a little late, Aichi.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.150
You still look sleepy.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:48.310
Yeah. I stayed up kind of late...

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.170
Yes, you did.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.350
So, did you learn anything?

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.330
W-Well...

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.700
When I try to make a new deck 
with just the cards I have now,

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.670
there really isn't any change in pattern...

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.150
Really?

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:11.260
That's because it hasn't been 
long since you started, Aichi.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.650
It can't be helped.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:13.620
Yeah...

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.790
Huh? Where are Kai and Mitsusada?

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.480
Those two...

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:28.140
They woke up earlier than anyone and have 
been fighting like that all morning.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.450
I see. So that's how 
you're coming after me...

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:36.170
You're still hiding something...

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:40.690
Both of you, it's time for breakfast.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:41.920
Okay...

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:46.670
If we don't all eat together, cleaning 
up afterwards will be a pain.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.670
Right. We'll eat a little bit later.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.100
Later?

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.430
Were you not listening to me?!

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.710
O-Of course I was!

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.530
Let's have breakfast as soon as 
this fight is over, all right?

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.330
Fine.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.900
G-Good.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.000
Um, it's your turn, right?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:05.710
Yeah.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.770
Good grief! I'm worried about your future.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:15.460
Results of the Training Camp

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.930
Hey, hey!

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.250
Curry for breakfast?!

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.930
There really wasn't much of a choice...

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.970
We have a lot left over from last night.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.420
I guess we got carried 
away and made too much...

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:30.170
Not to mention, somebody 
chopped a ton of onions...

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:31.560
Whatever.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.210
If we don't finish this off, 
it'll be curry for lunch, too!

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.350
Are you serious?!

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:38.430
Aichi, fill up!

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:43.640
I love curry, so I wouldn't 
mind it for lunch too!

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.320
Ah, youth...

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.980
H-Hey, aren't you gonna have any?!

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:05.530
I only have toast and tea for breakfast.

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.850
Th-That's not fair!

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:15.190
Well, everyone, you certainly did eat a lot.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:16.740
I couldn't have another bite...

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.470
Are you okay, Aichi?

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:24.120
What do you think? Head to the beach 
for a bit to settle your digestion?

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.510
That's right! We didn't come 
to the beach for nothing!

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:31.620
Today for sure, with all of my might...

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.100
I'm going swimming!

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.170
Aichi, did you bring your swimsuit?

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:38.250
H-Hey!

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:40.130
Uh uh. I burn really easily.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.350
Wait up! Hey!

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:50.870
Yahoo!

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.180
What the heck was that for, you little brat?!

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:07.590
Lose-umi, what are we here for again?

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.040
Um...

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:10.430
Swimming?

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:14.580
Wrong! This is a training 
camp! A card training camp!

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.910
Now that you remind me...

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:20.730
How could you totally forget that?

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:24.780
Listen! This is no time for fooling around!

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.200
Then what are we gonna do?

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.480
Thank you for asking, Brother!

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:32.230
In a word, what we should be doing is...

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:33.700
Special training!

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.050
Special training?

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:39.880
That's right! Our purpose is to defeat AL4!

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:43.390
And in order to do that, we're gonna 
do Vanguard Fight special training!

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.690
Special training...

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:48.670
I see! Special training, huh?

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.040
It looks like we're on the same page!

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:52.910
That's it! Special training!

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.690
Listen up! You need to work hard 
to give up the name "Lose-umi"

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:00.260
and get the name "Katsumi" back!

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:01.590
You can't just stand around!

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:02.960
Yes, Coach!

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:03.950
What are you?!

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.100
A Vanguard fighter!

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:08.090
Morikawa is a sucker for 
a passionate speech...

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.050
Are you the strongest?!

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:06.870
I'm the strongest!

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:07.500
Are you the strongest?!

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.300
I'm the strongest!

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:09.770
R-Really?

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:11.380
Then go! You're the wind! Become the wind!

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:13.510
Actually, those two are 
about the same mental age...

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.310
Yes, Coach!

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:19.300
Well, everyone, we're all here...

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.850
So how are we going to do "special training"?

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.060
We'll start with the most basic of 
the basics, taking a practice swing!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.100
Practice swing?

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:26.950
Right!

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:30.300
First, widen your stance a bit.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:32.260
Slowly lower your hips.

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.530
Then quietly draw your right hand back...

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:38.600
With your eyes fixed on your target,

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:41.420
like a hawk circling its prey...

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:43.460
Draw!

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:49.200
Draw!

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.650
Yes! That's the way you do it, Lose-umi!

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:54.290
I can't hear you!

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.230
D-Draw...

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.140
Brother!

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.100
Your hand is dropping.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.880
The finish should be diagonally 
forward, at a 45 degree angle!

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:12.910
Draw!

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:16.240
Okay! 100 more times!

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.050
No complaints!

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.030
Yes, sir!

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.930
All right, sound off!

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.290
1!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.500
1!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.490
2!

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:25.590
2!

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:26.630
3!

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:28.140
3!

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:30.740
They came to the beach to do that?

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.180
Really...

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:34.600
But, take a look. Over here, too...

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.590
99...

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.490
100!

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.090
That was tougher than I thought it'd be...

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.920
What, Lose-umi, complaining already?

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.120
What?! Not on your life!

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.080
Okay, next! What's our 
next training exercise?

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.180
There, that's the spirit!

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:56.580
Ready? The next special 
training exercise is...

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.140
The ride movement!

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.850
The ride movement?

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:04.170
How is that different from what we just did?

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.190
Where drawing is like an 
eagle seizing its prey,

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:10.380
riding is like an eagle 
tearing its enemy apart!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.390
An eagle, huh?! Okay, I got it!

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:15.450
Then sound off!

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:17.100
1!

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.180
1!

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.160
2!

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:19.950
2!

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.350
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.350
Stand up the Vanguard!

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.980
Basic physical fitness is also 
important in a Vanguard fight!

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:32.050
Push-ups, sit-ups, back 
stretches, 5 sets of 30 each!

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:33.300
Let's go!

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.630
1!

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.230
2!

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:37.680
3!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.610
I attack with my total power, 23000!

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.100
No guard.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.080
I did it!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:54.830
All right! Next!

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.230
Wait, Kamui!

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:58.730
What's wrong? Are you whining now?

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:00.010
No!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.540
There's something missing 
in your special training!

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.390
Say what?! What do you think is missing?!

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.850
What your special training doesn't have...

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.220
is imagination!

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:11.130
I-Imagination?!

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:15.860
That's right! In a Vanguard 
fight, the most important thing

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.810
is imagination!

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:21.160
This world is a melding of science and magic,

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.710
developed by a unique civilization!

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:26.560
Right now, a long-term war is going on,

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:29.300
and one Vanguard has landed 
on the planet to stop it!

00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:30.980
That Vanguard would be me...

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:35.360
the strongest fighter ever, Katsumi Morikawa!

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:37.450
I-I see!

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:39.590
I know what you mean, Morikawa!

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.030
Izaki, picture it!

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:43.330
You too, Kamui!

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:46.310
I-If you say so, Brother...

00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:56.670
P-Picture it!

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:58.510
Picture it...

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.490
Everyone! It's lunchtime!

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:08.800
Just what I've been waiting for!

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:11.970
Picture it, picture it, picture it...

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:16.580
Picture it, picture it, 
picture it, picture it...

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.530
Breakfast was heavy, so we're just 
having some cold noodles for lunch.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.530
And I appreciate it!

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:24.970
I'm physically and mentally 
exhausted, so this is perfect!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.100
It's making my whole body tingle.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:31.360
Listen, as soon as we're done eating, 
it's back to the special training!

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:34.760
Your training's grueling, 
but I'm not givin' in!

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:36.880
Special training, is it?

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:39.170
Then how about something like this?

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.900
Manager, what is this?!

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:53.750
My own card collection, which 
took many years to assemble!

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.450
Are these all Vanguard cards?

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:57.750
That's right!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:01.180
Just for today, I'll let 
you guys borrow them...

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:04.320
Hey! All of the grade 3 cards are mine!

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:06.640
What?!

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:08.750
Y-You can only borrow them!

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.300
That's my treasure, so...

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.430
Aichi...

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.290
Put out your right hand for a moment.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:18.950
Here.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.450
Those are Royal Paladin cards for you.

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:26.580
Th-Thank you!

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:34.250
Wow, there are a lot of cards 
here that I've never seen before!

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:35.280
What do you think?

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:40.010
As special training, why not use those 
as you like to put together a new deck?

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:41.680
As I like?

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:46.310
That's right. Try to give form 
to the image you have of winning.

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:51.310
I will!

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.090
You don't have enough grade 3s!

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:21.660
The more kinds of cards there are, the more 
I can do, the more I'm not sure what to do!

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:22.960
Aichi...

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.550
Aichi Sendou...

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:31.270
Grade 3! Grade 3, I say!

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:33.890
Don't tell me a card was...

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:39.700
No! That was only in my dream...

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:41.340
Aichi Sendou!

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:47.480
Our leader...

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:49.650
Aichi Sendou!

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:55.040
W-What is this?!

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.090
Th-This is...

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:48.270
Well, well!

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:51.460
It looks like you've put your deck together.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:58.570
Okay.

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:02.210
I'll check the deck's balance for you.

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:07.500
Great!

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:11.790
What have we here?

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:17.200
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:23.810
When did I put this deck together?

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:26.170
It's strange...

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:29.440
But for some reason, I feel like 
I can win with this deck...

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.530
What's wrong? You're starting.

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.940
Right, sorry!

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:39.860
I'm in the middle of a fight 
now. I have to concentrate!

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:40.770
Draw!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.940
I ride Little Sage, Marron!

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:46.540
Barcgal moves to the rear-guard.

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:49.430
Then, with Barcgal's skill, I call Flogal!

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:56.990
My turn is over.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:01.020
Well, so far this is a safe start.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:04.520
Whatever kind of deck you 
built, I'll see it in action.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.420
I ride Karenroid, Daisy.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:09.810
And then I call

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:11.640
one more Karenroid, Daisy!

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:18.020
I attack Marron with my Vanguard Daisy!

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:21.060
Drive check!

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:22.710
I got a trigger!

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:25.660
I give the critical +1 to my Vanguard Daisy.

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:29.360
Naturally, I give the power 
to my rear-guard, Daisy.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:34.380
I attack Marron with the powered-up Daisy.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:36.940
No guard.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.950
Damage trigger check!

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.450
Critical trigger!

00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:49.380
I give all the effects to Marron.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:52.480
But that's the end of my attack.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:55.960
Maybe drawing the trigger 
at this point was pointless.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.310
I stand and draw!

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:02.680
All right!

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:06.820
Stand up, my avatar!

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:07.760
I ride...

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.530
Blaster Blade!

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.680
But what should I do next?

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:23.230
Aichi, me!

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:28.040
I see!

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:31.530
I call High Dog Breeder, Akane!

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.700
High Dog Breeder, Akane?

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.570
That unit wasn't in his deck yesterday.

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:44.560
I pay the cost to activate Akane's skill!

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.660
I get to pick Pongal from my deck,

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.090
and superior call!

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:00.360
Pongal...

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:03.420
And then Pongal's Counterblast!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.270
This is...

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:32.190
I see. It looks like you've 
grabbed your image of how to win.

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:36.100
Yep!

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.090
This is my image of victory!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.600
So you've finally grabbed it, Aichi!

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:56.510
Well done!

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:58.970
That's my number one pupil!

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:00.680
M-Morikawa...

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.440
Therefore...

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:06.120
as you've moved up a rung, 
you'll have to fight me.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:07.950
But...

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:10.840
Just know that I'm not gonna go easy on you.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:13.860
Using Manager's cards increases the 
degree of my deck's mighty power,

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:16.740
so you'll be up against 
an ultra-powerful deck!

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.580
W-Wait a second.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:19.790
My fight isn't...

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:22.020
That's okay. I'll switch with him.

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:24.060
I understand your deck.

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:26.340
And it's a good one.

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.730
Th-Thank you!

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:30.350
Let's go, Aichi!

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:31.320
Okay!

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:34.270
The kids sure are restless, aren't they?

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:35.150
Yep.

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:37.230
But he's growing up quickly.

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:38.530
How's that?

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:41.380
Forming that deck in only one day.

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:43.550
That boy may have real talent.

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:46.890
Among that group, we might have to be careful

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:49.970
of more than Kai Toshiki.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.740
Team Quadrifoglio...

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:57.590
They're better rivals than I thought.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:01.270
Holding this training 
camp was the right idea.

00:21:05.720 --> 00:21:07.960
Everyone's on the bus, right?

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:09.380
We're pulling out!

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:10.590
Okay!

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:13.630
Mitsusada, Yuri, Gai...

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.800
Thank you! I've learned a lot!

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:18.400
It makes me happy to hear you say that.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:19.780
Let's meet again.

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:22.940
If possible, at the final fight 
of the national championship.

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:24.840
Right!

00:21:34.110 --> 00:21:36.160
Miss Emi, wanna play a card game?

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.780
They're all still kids...

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:50.360
Well, did you get something from this, Aichi?

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:58.020
I feel like I've forgotten something...

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:04.260
That's right! I never went swimming!

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:07.600
Manager! Go back! Take us 
right back to the beach!

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:09.770
I-I can't do that!

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:18.200
Let me swim in the sea!

00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:52.780
A deck made to win...

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:55.480
Everyone probably puts 
together a deck for that!

00:23:55.480 --> 00:23:59.800
I guess it's about a certain victory pattern, 
or bringing your opponent over to your stance.

00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:01.760
Huh! Sounds like you speak from experience.

00:24:01.760 --> 00:24:04.250
You're strong if you fight 
within your own space, right?

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:05.720
Like Kai, you know?

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:06.800
Right!

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:08.910
Next time: The King of Underground Fights!

00:24:08.910 --> 00:24:13.090
I bet Kai has a lot of images 
that he uses for winning.

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:15.590
Hmm, there are a lot of mysteries 
regarding his behavior.

00:24:15.590 --> 00:24:18.290
It kind of feels like if I don't stick 
with him, he'll get himself in trouble...
